    <h1 style="margin-top:14px">Interest in AI got <em>ahead of</em> the capacity to review it</h1>
    <p class="dek">One way I design a Responsible AI intake that people outside technology can answer, cheap enough that people use it, and built to follow a use case past its first assessment. Shown through an invented college.</p>
    <p class="tldr" data-aud="gen"><b>In short</b>Interest in AI use cases often grows faster than a central team can review them one at a time. My approach is a short self-assessment that the person responsible fills in themselves. Their answers decide which cases need an expert. It's an approach that has worked for me, not the only way to do it. The organization in it is invented.</p>
