            <span>Medium-risk</span><span class="cost"><span class="c-self">self-assessment</span></span>
            <span>High-risk</span><span class="cost"><span class="c-self">self-assessment</span><span class="c-exp">expert review</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="note"><span>Expert time goes where the answers point.</span><span class="cl inf">inferred</span><span>Cheap to declare, so small cases are more likely to be declared.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- THE INTAKE -->
<section class="wrap chapter" id="intake" aria-labelledby="h-intake">
  <div class="lens-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">The intake</p>
    <h2 id="h-intake">An intake anyone responsible for a use case can answer</h2>
    <div class="minilife" role="img" aria-label="Where this chapter sits in a use case's life: the intake and the assessment"><span class="ml-line"><span class="ml-s"><i></i>requested</span><span class="ml-s on"><i></i>intake</span><span class="ml-s on"><i></i>assessed</span><span class="ml-s"><i></i>reassessed</span></span><span class="ml-label">the intake and the assessment</span></div>
    <p>One front door, one self-assessment, and an answer for every submission.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="scrolly">
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step" data-step="0" id="s-in-0"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Principles</p>
        <h3>Principles as everyday expectations</h3>
        <p>I start from the organization's own principles, turn each one into an everyday expectation, and give people a single self-assessment as the way in.</p>
        <p>Wrenfield's five, invented for this page: fairness, transparency, accountability, privacy and safety.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="1" id="s-in-1"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">The assessment</p>
        <h3>Questions about the work, not the technology</h3>
        <p>Most questions are yes or no. They ask what the AI does, who uses it, what data it touches and what decisions it informs.</p>
        <p>A privacy screen sits alongside the principles, so privacy can follow up whatever the review path.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="2" id="s-in-2"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Describing a use case</p>
        <h3>A fill-in pattern and a worked example</h3>
        <p>Guidance with a fill-in pattern and a worked example steers people towards plain-language descriptions that make human oversight, personal data and impact on people visible, and away from technical architecture.</p>
        <p>I use an AI assistant to check that guidance reads clearly to someone outside technology.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="3" id="s-in-3"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Triage</p>
        <h3>Every submission gets an answer</h3>
        <p>A workflow gives each submission a reference number, applies the rules<span class="gloss" data-aud="gen"> (the logic that turns answers into a review path)</span>, and sends the submitter a notice: the review path, the reasoning and the next steps.</p>
        <p>Expert review follows only when the answers call for it.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="graphic">
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="flow">
          <div class="stage dim" data-on="0"><span class="who sys">Front</span><span class="t">Principles, one self-assessment <span class="fict">(invented)</span>
            <span class="chips"><span class="chip">fairness</span><span class="chip">transparency</span><span class="chip">accountability</span><span class="chip">privacy</span><span class="chip">safety</span></span></span></div>
          <div class="stage dim" data-on="1"><span class="who you">Sponsor</span><span class="t">Answer mostly yes/no questions
            <span class="chips"><span class="chip">what it does</span><span class="chip">who uses it</span><span class="chip">data it touches</span><span class="chip">decisions it informs</span><span class="chip">privacy screen</span></span></span></div>
          <div class="stage dim" data-on="2"><span class="who you">Sponsor</span><span class="t">Describe it in plain language
            <span class="chips"><span class="chip">human oversight</span><span class="chip">personal data</span><span class="chip">impact on people</span><span class="chip ai">clarity checked with AI</span></span></span></div>
          <div class="stage dim" data-on="3"><span class="who sys">Flow</span><span class="t">Reference number, then rules</span></div>
          <div class="stage dim" data-on="3"><span class="who sys">Notice</span><span class="t">Review path, reasoning and next steps</span></div>
