  </div>
</section>

<!-- HONEST ANSWERS -->
<section class="wrap chapter" id="answers" aria-labelledby="h-ans">
  <div class="lens-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Honest answers</p>
    <h2 id="h-ans">Designing for answers people can actually give</h2>
    <div class="minilife" role="img" aria-label="Where this chapter sits in a use case's life: an assessment, as Wrenfield runs it"><span class="ml-line"><span class="ml-s"><i></i>requested</span><span class="ml-s"><i></i>intake</span><span class="ml-s on"><i></i>assessed</span><span class="ml-s"><i></i>reassessed</span></span><span class="ml-label">an assessment, as Wrenfield runs it</span></div>
    <p>Three ideas I build into the assessment itself. The panel lets you try them.</p>
    <p class="disclose"><b>Everything here is invented.</b> Wrenfield, its questions, field names, rules and review paths are made up for this page. Nothing you choose leaves this page.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="scrolly inline">
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step" data-step="0" id="s-ans-0"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Review paths</p>
        <h3>The answers set the path, not the person</h3>
        <p>Wrenfield's rules work out a review path from the answers: self-serve, light review or full review. On any path, answers can also send the use case to privacy. The submitter never picks their own path.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="1" id="s-ans-1"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Unsure</p>
        <h3>“Unsure” is a signal that needs review</h3>
        <p>An unsure answer isn't counted as a no. The system names the specific questions the submitter was unsure about, so reviewers have something concrete to follow up.</p>
        <p>Set an answer the rules depend on to Unsure, such as whether it informs decisions about students, and the path becomes a range instead of a guess.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="2" id="s-ans-2"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Stated vs computed</p>
        <h3>What people said, kept apart from what the system worked out</h3>
        <p>I keep what the person said apart from what the system worked out, with a naming convention for fields, so the line between them stays visible in the record.</p>
        <p data-aud="gen">In the panel, the left column is what the person said and the right column is what the system worked out.</p>
        <p data-aud="pro">The panel shows the idea with <code>answer.*</code> and <code>derived.*</code> prefixes, invented for this page.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="graphic">
      <div class="panel" id="assess">
        <div class="panel-head"><span class="lab">The pattern · invented questions</span></div>
        <div id="toyForm" class="hlz" data-on="1" role="group" aria-label="Invented assessment questions"></div>
        <ul class="nojs-q" aria-label="Invented questions, with this example's answers"><li>Is it already in use? <b>Yes</b></li><li>Does it inform decisions about students or applicants? <b>Yes</b></li><li>Does a person review its output before anyone acts on it? <b>Yes</b></li><li>Does it use personal information? <b>Unsure</b></li><li>Will students or the public interact with it directly? <b>No</b></li></ul>
        <div class="rstrip hlz" data-on="0" id="rstrip">
          <div class="rs-top"><span class="lab">Result</span><b class="rs-level" data-ltext="">Light review</b></div>
          <div class="lvlbar" aria-hidden="true"><span data-l="self">Self-serve</span><span data-l="light" class="cur">Light</span><span data-l="full">Full</span></div>
          <div class="rs-pills"><span class="pill rev" data-pill="priv">Privacy: follow-up</span><span class="pill flag" data-pill="exp">Expert review: triggered</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="sr" role="status" id="rStatus"></p>
        <p class="review hlz" data-on="1" id="reviewLine">Unsure on: Does it use personal information? Each one goes to a reviewer to follow up.</p>
        <p class="retro" id="retroLine">You've just assessed something already running. That's an assessment after the fact.</p>
        <div class="result">
          <div class="col stated hlz" data-on="2"><p class="lab"><span data-aud="pro">answer</span><span data-aud="gen">what the person said</span></p><ul id="statedList"><li><span data-aud="pro">answer.already_in_use = </span><span data-aud="gen">Already in use: </span><span>yes</span></li><li><span data-aud="pro">answer.student_decisions = </span><span data-aud="gen">Informs decisions about students: </span><span>yes</span></li><li><span data-aud="pro">answer.human_review = </span><span data-aud="gen">A person reviews output first: </span><span>yes</span></li><li><span data-aud="pro">answer.personal_data = </span><span data-aud="gen">Uses personal information: </span><span class="v-review">unsure</span></li><li><span data-aud="pro">answer.public_facing = </span><span data-aud="gen">Students use it directly: </span><span>no</span></li></ul></div>
          <div class="col hlz" data-on="2"><p class="lab"><span data-aud="pro">derived</span><span data-aud="gen">what the system worked out</span></p><ul id="compList"><li><span data-aud="pro">derived.review_path = </span><span data-aud="gen">Review path: </span><span class="v-flag">light review</span></li><li><span data-aud="pro">derived.privacy_routing = </span><span data-aud="gen">Privacy routing: </span><span class="v-review">follow-up</span></li><li><span data-aud="pro">derived.expert_review = </span><span data-aud="gen">Expert review: </span><span class="v-flag">triggered</span></li></ul></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="notice-out" id="ans-notice">
    <div class="notice-lede"><p class="kicker">The notice</p><h3>What the submitter gets back</h3><p>This is the notice your answers above would send: a reference number, a review path, the reasons and the next steps. Change an answer and it rewrites itself.</p></div>
    <div class="notice">
          <p class="lab">The notice this would send · invented</p>
