<!-- BY RESPONSIBILITY -->
<section class="wrap chapter" id="architecture" aria-labelledby="h-arch">
  <div class="lens-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">By responsibility</p>
    <h2 id="h-arch">Documented by what each part is responsible for</h2>
    <div class="minilife" role="img" aria-label="Where this chapter sits in a use case's life: inside one assessment"><span class="ml-line"><span class="ml-s"><i></i>requested</span><span class="ml-s"><i></i>intake</span><span class="ml-s on"><i></i>assessed</span><span class="ml-s"><i></i>reassessed</span></span><span class="ml-label">inside one assessment</span></div>
    <p>I describe a service by what each part is responsible for, not by which platform it runs on, and label each part as verified, documented or planned.</p>
    <p class="sr" role="status" id="swStatus"></p>
  </div>
  <div class="scrolly">
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step" data-step="0" id="s-arch-0"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">The swap test</p>
        <h3>The meaning lives in the decision logic</h3>
        <p><span class="cl inf">inferred</span>Replacing the workflow tool would barely change the service. Replacing the decision logic would make it a different service.</p>
        <p data-aud="gen">In plain terms: the tool that moves the form around matters much less than the rules that decide the path.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="1" id="s-arch-1"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Authority</p>
        <h3>Authority assigned per piece of information</h3>
        <p>I map which part holds authority for each kind of information: the original response, the computed result, the governance record and the notice sent.</p>
        <p>No single system gets labelled the source of truth for everything.</p>
        <p data-aud="gen">For each kind of record, exactly one place holds the official copy.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="2" id="s-arch-2"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Status labels</p>
        <h3>A record that says how sure it is</h3>
        <p>Every claim in the architecture record carries a status: verified, documented or planned.</p>
        <p>The record stays provisional until it's checked against the running system.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="graphic">
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="sec dim" data-on="0">
          <span class="lab">Swap test · invented · <span class="cl inf">inferred</span></span>
          <div class="pipe">
            <span class="pk">Your answers</span><span class="marks" data-swmarks="" role="img" aria-label="Your answers: Already in use, yes; Informs decisions about students, yes; A person reviews output first, yes; Uses personal information, unsure; Students use it directly, no"><span class="mk yes" title="Is it already in use? yes">Y</span><span class="mk yes" title="Does it inform decisions about students or applicants? yes">Y</span><span class="mk yes" title="Does a person review its output before anyone acts on it? yes">Y</span><span class="mk unsure" title="Does it use personal information? unsure">?</span><span class="mk no" title="Will students or the public interact with it directly? no">N</span></span>
            <span class="ar" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
            <span class="pk">Workflow tool</span><span class="seg2"><button type="button" data-swap="tool" data-v="a">Tool A</button><button type="button" data-swap="tool" data-v="b">Tool B</button></span>
            <span class="ar" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
            <span class="pk">Decision rules</span><span class="seg2"><button type="button" data-swap="rules" data-v="a">Current</button><button type="button" data-swap="rules" data-v="b">Alternative</button></span>
            <span class="ar" aria-hidden="true">=</span>
            <span class="pk">Review path</span><span class="swout" data-swapout="">Light review</span>
          </div>
          <p class="swapnote" data-swapnote="">The current setup. Swap the tool, then the rules.</p>
          <p class="swaphint">Swap one part at a time. <a href="#assess">Edit your answers <span aria-hidden="true">↑</span></a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="sec dim" data-on="1">
          <span class="lab">Authority by information type</span>
          <div class="chips"><span class="chip">original response</span><span class="chip">computed result</span><span class="chip">governance record</span><span class="chip">notice sent</span></div>
          <div class="flowline" style="margin-top:8px"><span class="arrowtxt" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="chip ink">one authoritative home for each</span></div>
          <p class="struck">one source of truth for everything</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sec dim" data-on="2">
          <span class="lab">Architecture record · component status</span>
          <div class="cstat"><span class="v">verified</span><span>documented</span><span class="p">planned</span></div>
          <div class="chips" style="margin-top:6px"><span class="chip flag">provisional until checked against the running system</span></div>
          <p class="selfref">This page does the same to itself. Its main claims are graded in <a href="#claims">What it can claim <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></p>
          <div class="chips"><span class="cl">observed</span><span class="cl doc">document-supported</span><span class="cl inf">inferred</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- BETWEEN ASSESSMENTS -->
<section class="wrap chapter" id="between" aria-labelledby="h-btw">
  <div class="lens-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Between assessments</p>
    <h2 id="h-btw">A use case outlives its first assessment</h2>
    <div class="minilife" role="img" aria-label="Where this chapter sits in a use case's life: after the notice, and between assessments"><span class="ml-line"><span class="ml-s"><i></i>requested</span><span class="ml-s"><i></i>intake</span><span class="ml-s on"><i></i>assessed</span><span class="ml-s on"><i></i>reassessed</span></span><span class="ml-label">after the notice, and between assessments</span></div>
    <p>Two questions I ask of any intake before it launches. Both are about what it keeps once it has answered.</p>
    <p class="sr" role="status" id="btwStatus"></p>
  </div>
  <div class="scrolly">
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step" data-step="0" id="s-btw-0"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Identity</p>
        <h3>Can it tell this is the same use case?</h3>
        <p>A reference number names a submission, not the use case. Without a lasting ID that follows a use case through every assessment, a reassessment can't be linked back to the earlier one.</p>
        <p>Without that link, an intake stays a queue of submissions instead of becoming an inventory. Try it with the notice you got above.</p>
        <p data-aud="pro">What an inventory record adds: a persistent ID, plus the overview, data, logic and governance details that public AI registers publish for each system, kept up to date as it changes.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="1" id="s-btw-1"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Decisions</p>
        <h3>Does it keep what the reviewer decided?</h3>
        <p>The rules produce a recommendation. A person makes the decision. I record both with the use case, because an intake that keeps only its recommendation can't show whether its routing works.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="graphic">
      <div class="panel gaps">
        <svg class="gapline g1" viewBox="0 0 360 92" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Two design questions placed on a use case's timeline: identity between assessments, and the review decision after the notice.">
          <path class="gl-base" d="M14 52 H346"/>
          <circle class="gl-pt" cx="40" cy="52" r="4"/><text x="40" y="78" text-anchor="middle">intake</text>
          <circle class="gl-pt" cx="130" cy="52" r="5"/><text x="130" y="78" text-anchor="middle">assessed</text>
          <circle class="gl-pt" cx="200" cy="52" r="4"/><text x="200" y="78" text-anchor="middle">notice</text>
          <circle class="gl-pt" cx="318" cy="52" r="5"/><text x="318" y="78" text-anchor="middle">reassessed</text>
          <path class="gl-arc" d="M140 48 Q228 -28 316 48"/>
          <g class="gm m2"><circle cx="200" cy="32" r="9"/><text x="200" y="36" text-anchor="middle">2</text></g>
          <g class="gm m1"><circle cx="228" cy="11" r="9"/><text x="228" y="15" text-anchor="middle">1</text></g>
        </svg>
        <div class="gapcard dim" data-on="0,1">
          <h4><span class="gnum">1</span> <span class="chip">identity</span> Same use case, new reference</h4>
          <div class="mini reassess dim done" data-on="0">
            <div class="rgrid">
              <div class="rcard"><p class="rc-k">Your notice</p><p class="rc-ref" data-ra-ref="">REF-4478</p><p class="rc-sum" data-ra-sum="">Light review · privacy follow-up</p><p class="rc-id">use-case ID <span>none</span></p></div>
              <div class="rlink" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 22"><path class="rl-arc" d="M2 20 Q20 -6 38 20"/></svg><span>no link</span></div>
              <div class="rcard b">
                <div class="rb-empty"><button type="button" class="rbtn" data-reassess>Reassess it, a year later</button><p class="rc-k">your answers, plus one change</p></div>
                <div class="rb-full"><p class="rc-k">A year later</p><p class="rc-ref" data-rb-ref="">REF-5509</p><p class="rc-sum" data-rb-sum="">Full review · privacy follow-up</p><p class="rc-chg" data-rb-change="">Since then (invented): nobody reviews its output first.</p><p class="rc-id">use-case ID <span>none</span></p></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="rmsg" data-rmsg="">To you, it's the same use case. To the record, REF-4478 and REF-5509 are two unrelated submissions. Its path moved from light review to full review, and nothing here can connect the two.</p>
            <p class="rmsg" data-aud="pro">An inventory record would carry one persistent ID across both.</p>
            <button type="button" class="rreset" data-reassess-reset>Start over</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="gapcard dim" data-on="0,1">
          <h4><span class="gnum">2</span> <span class="chip">decision</span> Recommendation, then decision</h4>
          <div class="mini flowline dim" data-on="1">
            <span class="chip">recommendation computed</span><span class="arrowtxt" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="chip ink">reviewer decides</span><span class="arrowtxt" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="chip blue">both kept with the use case</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

<section class="wrap outcome" id="outcome" aria-labelledby="oc-h">
  <p class="eyebrow">What it's for</p>
  <h2 id="oc-h" style="margin-top:8px">An intake people use, built to follow a use case through its life</h2>
  <div class="oc-grid two">
    <div>
      <h3>Cheap to declare</h3>
      <p>The person responsible answers for their own work, gets a notice straight away, and expert time goes where the answers point.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Built for the second assessment</h3>
      <p>A persistent use-case ID and a recorded review decision, so over time the intake becomes an inventory.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="reflect">An assessment is an event, but a use case has a life. <span>I design the intake to model both.</span></p>
</section>

<section class="wrap claims" id="claims" aria-labelledby="h-claims">
